      "notes": "**Caris Life Sciences (CAI), news from 2026-09-29 to 2026-10-29**\n\n**1. Guidance and results**\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or new results fell in the window. The last guidance move was on 2026-08-05, when Caris \nraised 2026 revenue guidance to $1.03–1.04 billion, growth of 27% to 28%\n. — 2026-08-05 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002019410/000201941026000053/cai_ex99-1.htm\n- Management said the raise \ndoes not include any contribution from new products such as Caris Detect, ChromoSeq or MI Clarity V2\n. — 2026-08-05 — https://www.investing.com/news/transcripts/earnings-call-transcript-caris-life-sciences-tops-q2-2026-revenue-forecast-shares-jump-93CH-4839607\n- Q3 guidance on the same call: \nblended clinical average selling price in the $3,800–$3,900 range\n. — 2026-08-05 — same URL\n- \nCaris will report Q3 2026 results on November 4, 2026\n. The date was announced on 2026-10-15. — 2026-10-15 — https://investor.carislifesciences.com/news-releases/news-release-details/caris-life-sciences-report-third-quarter-2026-financial-results\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- BTIG raised its target to $38 from $33 and kept Buy, in a Q3 sector preview. — 2026-10-27 (per rallies.ai) — https://www.tipranks.com/news/the-fly/caris-life-sciences-price-target-raised-to-38-from-33-at-btig-thefly-news and https://rallies.ai/news/caris-life-sciences-target-price-raised-to-38-from-33-69438d6c3ceb04d8\n  - A CNN listing of the same item reads \"Yesterday,\" which points to 10-28. — https://www.cnn.com/markets/stocks/CAI\n- Canaccord Genuity raised its target to $30 from $22 and kept Hold. The sources disagree on the date:\n  - \nMarketBeat: research note on Monday\n. — 2026-10-19 — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/analyst-caris-life-sciences-nasdaq-cai-price-target-raised-to-3000-2026-10-19/\n  - \nGuruFocus: October 14, 2026\n. — 2026-10-14 — https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9129688/cai-maintained-by-canaccord-genuity-price-target-raised-to-30\n- JPMorgan raised its target to $35 from $25 and kept Overweight. — 2026-10-14 — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/analyst-caris-life-sciences-nasdaq-cai-stock-price-target-raised-at-jpmorgan-chase-co-2026-10-14/\n- TD Cowen raised its target to $36 from $30 and kept Buy. — 2026-10-13 — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CAI/price-targets\n- BofA raised its target to $35 from $23. — 2026-10-09 (per CNN's timestamp) — https://www.cnn.com/markets/stocks/CAI\n- Weiss Ratings \ncut Caris from \"sell (d+)\" to \"sell (d)\"\n. — 2026-10-02 — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/analyst-caris-life-sciences-nasdaq-cai-price-target-raised-to-3000-2026-10-19/\n- Consensus per MarketBeat: \neight buy, five hold and one sell among 14 analysts\n. The average target is $27.82. — as of 2026-10-18 — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/consensus-caris-life-sciences-inc-nasdaq-cai-stock-has-average-target-price-of-2782-according-to-brokerages-2026-10-18/\n  - The $27.82 average does not include the Oct 19 Canaccord and Oct 27 BTIG changes. MarketBeat's Oct 19 article gives a consensus target of $28.55. — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/analyst-caris-life-sciences-nasdaq-cai-price-target-raised-to-3000-2026-10-19/\n\n**3. Litigation and regulation**\n- Nothing new in the window. The latest 10-Q on file (quarter ended June 30) describes a DOJ False Claims Act civil investigative demand received in March 2025 over Medicare's 14-day rule. \nThe investigation is at too early a stage to assess outcomes, and Caris is cooperating.\n — event date 2025-03 (CID received) — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002019410/000201941026000055/cai-20260630.htm\n- I found no new Caris approvals, fines or antitrust matters in the window.\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- I found nothing material on customer wins, losses or contract changes in the window, and no concentration disclosure was surfaced.\n\n**5. Insider activity**\n- I found no Form 4 with a transaction date inside 2026-09-29 to 2026-10-29.\n- Sales just before the window, relevant to clustering (MarketBeat counts \nabout 1 million shares worth $27.2 million sold over the past 90 days\n):\n  - President David Spetzler exercised 1.25M options at $2.44 and sold 597,212 shares at about $24.76–$25.32. These were broker-assisted sell-to-cover sales on options expiring 2026-09-12. — 2026-09-03 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/CAI/form-4-caris-life-sciences-inc-insider-trading-activity-8b4a09de1056.html and https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002019410/000207195326000007/wk-form4_1788555596.xml\n  - Director and officer Brian Brille exercised 400,000 options and sold 400,000 shares at $30.33. — 2026-09-17 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002019410/000207195926000008/wk-form4_1789682909.xml\n  - General Counsel John Russel Denton sold 7,500 shares at $31.82. — 2026-09-22 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002019410/000207192326000007/wk-form4_1790197601.xml\n- The sources reviewed do not say whether any of these sales were under a 10b5-1 plan.\n\n**6. Product and competitive news**\n- Caris launched a national TV commercial featuring Jordan Spieth on early-stage cancer detection. — 2026-10-19 — https://investor.carislifesciences.com/news-events/news-releases\n- Caris announced eight posters at ESMO 2026, which ran \nOctober 23-27, 2026, in Madrid\n. — 2026-10-14 — https://www.carislifesciences.com/about/news-and-media/caris-life-sciences-to-present-eight-studies-highlighting-the-power-of-ai-multi-omics-and-precision-medicine-at-esmo-2026/\n- A similar commercial featuring Kevin Costner, tied to Caris Detect, is listed on the IR page. — date unknown — https://investor.carislifesciences.com/news-events/news-releases\n- Competitor GRAIL's Galleri test is moving toward FDA approval. An FDA advisory panel \nvoted 7 to 2, with one abstention, that benefits outweigh risks\n. The vote was just before the window and bears on Caris Detect. — 2026-09-23 —